    "body": "I did talk to Qualcomm legal about this. The summary is that they asked we do not remove Qualcomm from the copyright statement in the LICENSE (or any other) file.*** [BEGIN THIS IS NOT LEGAL ADVICE] Apparently, the copyright statement has very little effect on IP protections anyway, and practically the git history tracks who owns the copyright for a given character [END THIS IS NOT LEGAL ADVICE]\r\n\r\nWe could track contributors, though that seems like a lot of overhead, especially it the git log is doing it anyway. FWIW, I put this is the draft on #571:\r\n\r\n```\r\nAll contributions to UnifiedDB are by default made under the xref:LICENSE[BSD-3-clear license].\r\nCopyrights are held by the specific contributors, and are not tracked by the UnifiedDB project other\r\nthan what can be gleaned through git history\r\n```\r\n\r\n*** Though Qualcomm is changing the legal entity that interacts with open source, so the new line is supposed to be \"Copyright (c) Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. and/or its subsidiaries.\" (Note: there is no 'All rights reserved' and no year)",
