    "commit_id": "8a8ec897311325ad32a93c99975cefcf2b421fb7",
    "original_commit_id": "915791b6ac14d140296b0dcbc8d636e91b588667",
    "user": null,
    "body": "I just pushed another change.  Basically adding this to the copyright statement in reuse.toml: `\"2024-2025 Contributors to the RISCV UnifiedDB <https://github.com/riscv-software-src/riscv-unified-db>\"` for the files that are UDB specific.\r\n\r\nMy thought process (as an engineer, not a lawyer) is trying to represent the lineage of the project where it started in Qualcomm and then was open sourced so now the contributions to the OSS project are under that blanket \"Contributors to the RISCV UnifiedDB\".  Now I'm wondering if I should add that to the license file under Qualcomm's blurb.\r\n\r\n@dhower-qc : I'll leave you to change the actual Qualcomm text to the new one you described if you want.\r\n\r\n",
